    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math somewhat distant, especially compared to biology or chemistry, which I enjoy more. I used to struggle with it in school, and my parents didn’t support my interest in it. Now, I see it as a tool—useful but not something I connect with emotionally. I appreciate its logic, but it doesn’t spark joy like science does.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, sometimes. When I have to solve something complex or when I feel I’m falling behind, I get a little nervous. It’s not panic, but a quiet worry that I might not understand. I try to calm myself with breathing and reminding myself that everyone has their own pace. I’m not afraid of math, just the pressure of not getting it right.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used a simple AI app to check my homework on algebra. It was helpful for basic problems, but I found it too rigid. It didn’t explain steps clearly, and I missed the reasoning behind the solutions. Still, it saved time when I was stuck. I’d prefer a tool that teaches like a teacher, not just gives answers.",
